# Evidence reading quality

For implementation details relevant to the assigned question, read the complete relevant functions and follow their inputs, assignments, called modules and configuration within the materials granted to this stage. For each conclusion about a value's origin, write its assignment chain from the original input in the Note and check the named operands against the cited lines. Preserve the actual input representation, length source and tensor layout; do not substitute what the algorithm's name or a comment suggests.

Include the implementation branches enabled by the selected configuration. Distinguish constructor defaults, example configurations and the configuration actually selected by the caller. If that selection is unknown, describe the supported branches conditionally. Separate equal tensor lengths from semantic alignment, and distinguish code-derived shapes from assumptions. An omitted Note or excerpt does not establish that the available Source lacks the detail.

Keep conclusions tied to the repository and version actually read. When combining materials within this stage's scope, identify their distinct origins and verify the relevant call chain before transferring a fact between them; one matching function or file does not establish that their callers and configuration agree. Preserve meaningful disagreements rather than silently merging them.

When compressing a Note, retain the assignment chains, branch conditions, configuration choices and qualifications needed for the requested detail. Concision must not remove evidence needed to reconstruct that conclusion. Stay within the stage's assigned Source scope; a limitation of these materials is not a judgment about other Sources or global coverage.
